1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,600
Phantom Ledger. A ghost ledger —
no account, no server, no trace.
Built for Kiroween 2026, Frankenstein category.

2
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:14,700
Community treasurers — for neighbourhoods,
mosques, or savings groups — usually track
cash in a paper notebook.

3
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:20,000
Phantom Ledger replaces it with an app
that lives entirely on your phone.
No sign-up, no login, no internet.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,700
Everything is stored locally, and categories
fill in automatically. Type "pay electricity",
and the category is already Electricity.

5
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:32,000
Hands busy? Just speak. Say:
expense, fifty thousand rupiah, for electricity.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,700
The app turns your voice into a transaction draft —
amount, type, and category already filled in.
You review it first, then save. Voice never writes directly.

7
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:46,000
This is the ghostliest part. There's no server —
so how do you move phones? With a QR code.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:55,100
One phone shows the code, the other scans it —
the whole ledger moves over, and matching records
merge automatically, with no duplicates.
No account, no cable, no cloud.

9
00:00:55,200 --> 00:01:01,500
At month's end, the report is ready in one tap.
Opening balance, income, expenses, per category.

10
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:08,200
Copied as WhatsApp text for the neighbourhood group,
or downloaded as CSV for the archive.

11
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:13,500
Phantom Ledger. Five technologies that
should never have met, stitched into one ledger.

12
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:19,600
Built with Kiro: specs, steering, and hooks.
Try it yourself — all the code is on GitHub.
